  "final_message": "Task 1 is done and recorded in the ledger: `Task 1: complete (commits 8c509a9..eab66a1, mutants: 3/3, tests: \u2026pytest -q \u2192 3 passed)`. `task-done` accepted it on the first try.\n\n- **What was missing:** in the first mutant run, mutant 2 survived. That mutant gives every left-over cent to the first person. The only test with cents left over was `split(1000, 3)`, which has just one, so the wrong code still passed.\n- **Fix:** I added `test_several_cents_left_over_go_one_each_to_the_first_people`, which checks that `split(1102, 4) == [276, 276, 275, 275]`. I left the plan's two tests unchanged. I also added a row for this case to `task-1-mutants.md` and pointed mutant 2 at the new test. The new test is commit `eab66a1`, with the trailers `Mutant-step: task 1 survivor 2` and `Mutant-step: task 1 input shape`.\n- **Reruns:** a quick re-check of the mutants the first run hadn't caught showed none surviving. The last full run, `.sdd/plan/task-1-mutants-2.log`, caught all 3 mutants with none invalid, at HEAD.\n- **Tests without the task's code:** with `bills.py` removed, the test file can't import it, so all three tests fail. Nothing more was needed there.\n\nI did not start the final review.",
